+## Abandoned orders (the list in /backends)
+
+`abandoned.php` (an include of `admin.php`; the table is `abandoned.mysql.sql`, repeated in
+`schema.mysql.sql`) answers two routes: `GET ?r=abandoned_orders` (the list and its summary)
+and `POST ?r=abandoned_followup` (the owner's own note on an order). Both need the admin
+session and `X-Sporta-Admin: 1`; reads are 90 a minute, writes 30. The list changes no order,
+no stock and no discount use; the one thing written is the owner's follow-up
+(`contacted`, `not_interested`, `wrong_number`, `recovered_manually`, a note of at most 280
+characters, who and when), one row per order, by one atomic upsert. Nothing is ever sent to
+a customer from the server: the WhatsApp link is built in the browser.
+
+What counts, read from the code that makes the states (`api.php` create_order, the bank
+callbacks, `cron-stock.php`, `store_stock_release`):
+
+- **unpaid**: a KNET / T-Pay order still pending after `abandoned_after_minutes` (default 30,
+  at least 5, never later than the sweeper's hold `stock_hold_minutes`, default 120).
+- **expired**: a card order whose hold has run out (the sweeper has put the stock back, or
+  will within 15 minutes), or one cancelled only after that.
+- **declined**: the bank refused it, or the shopper backed out at the gateway (`failed`).
+- **cod_expired**: a cash order nobody confirmed for `cod_hold_hours` (24), or cancelled only
+  after that. The sweeper cancels such an order and a person cancelling writes the same
+  thing; the order's timeline (`order_tracking_events`) says WHEN, and the sweeper can only act
+  after the hold, so a cancel before it is "cancelled" (a person's decision, not listed).
+- **waiting** (inside the threshold) and **cancelled** (by the shop before the hold ran out)
+  are counted apart and listed only on request.
+- Never listed: paid; `review` (the money may be real); a packed card order; a cash order inside
+  its hold or packed, shipped, delivered, paid; a cash order whose status is `failed` (the
+  historic import's wording).
+- **Recovered**: a later paid order, or a later cash order the shop has packed or shipped, from
+  the same phone or the same signed-in account (orders hold no email; `customer_accounts.email`
+  is unique, so one email is one account); or a follow-up marked `recovered_manually`.
+  Hidden by default, always counted.
+
+A shopper who never reached order creation is not recorded anywhere (the cart lives only in
+their browser), so cannot be listed; counting them would need a tracking beacon, which is the
+owner's privacy decision. `npm run test:abandoned-orders` proves all of the above on a private
+MariaDB, including the real sweeper and EXPLAIN at 20,000 orders.
+
